#====================================================================
# Draft - Neovim headless + Vusted/Busted upstream test chain
#====================================================================

id:                     E445
trigger_tool:           conan|neovim|vusted|busted|test_package
phase:                  testing|runtime
error_signature:        vusted ./test|make test -> vusted ./test|nvim --headless|0/9 actual upstream Vusted tests executed

severity:               2
category:               lua, testing, busted, neovim, path-b
match_keywords:         Neovim, nvim-lspconfig, vusted, busted, upstream test, headless, Path B, Lua runtime plugin, test_package
title:                  Neovim runtime plugins need a packaged Vusted/Busted chain for Path B upstream tests

root_cause:             Neovim runtime-plugin upstream tests can require a real headless Neovim plus Vusted/Busted Lua test harness; package-layout or Python consumer checks do not execute the upstream Vusted cases and must not be counted as upstream passes.
affected_scope:         Neovim Lua plugins whose upstream test entry is make test or vusted and whose OHOS validation depends on separately packaged neovim, vusted, busted, and Lua runtime modules.
verification_cmd:       From the packaged plugin root, run vusted ./test with packaged neovim and vusted in the Conan run environment, then record the upstream case count and full package refs.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           path-b-packaged-neovim-vusted-chain
rec_description:        Use Path B when the upstream test harness needs packaged Neovim/Vusted prerequisites; package the upstream test tree, run the real vusted command from the installed plugin root, and keep adapted consumer layout checks separate from upstream-test accounting.
rec_command:            conan create archives/n/nvim-lspconfig/2.5.0 --build=missing; cd <package>/share/nvim-lspconfig && vusted ./test
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               recipe-and-test-package

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      consumer-layout-guard-only
fallback_description:   If packaged Neovim/Vusted is unavailable, keep a Python or shell consumer check only as package layout validation and report upstream Vusted execution as 0/N.
fallback_command:       python test_package/test_nvim_lspconfig.py
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          manual-validation

forbid_1_pattern:       count.*Python.*layout.*upstream|count.*test_package.*as.*Vusted|claim.*Path A.*without.*vusted
forbid_1_reason:        Adapted consumer checks prove packaged files and selected behavior inputs but do not execute upstream Vusted/Busted cases.
forbid_1_consequence:   PR evidence can overstate upstream-test coverage and hide missing Neovim/Vusted runtime prerequisites.

forbid_2_pattern:       omit.*test/|omit.*lsp/|run.*vusted.*outside.*packaged.*root
forbid_2_reason:        nvim-lspconfig tests import both upstream test fixtures and runtime lsp files from the plugin root.
forbid_2_consequence:   The test command may validate a source checkout or incomplete package layout instead of the published artifact.

doc_file:               drafts/DRAFT-neovim-vusted-busted-upstream-test-chain.md
last_updated:           2026-08-24
source_event:           MR !3752 nvim-lspconfig/2.5.0 Path B knowledge extension

authors: zxyAtom <alhvrlVUxiGd6QEv.zxyAtom@noreply.gitcode.com>
source_pr: !3752
source_commit:

metrics_success_count:  1
metrics_fail_count:     0
metrics_confidence:     1.0
metrics_last_used:      2026-08-07

